r, a thread started by code under test) would burn the 10 s bound and fail the test spuriously. That replaces one flake with another.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1db98f60b3522019","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — `_drive_on_fresh_thread` join step","norm_id":"nbb8b7abffaae253c","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A pytest plugin or lazily-started library thread spawns during the drive window under `make verify` load."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Compute `new = [t for t in threading.enumerate() if t not in before and isinstance(t, anyio._backends._asyncio.WorkerThread)]`, join each, then `del new` before returning the weakref.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Guard the regression test on the presence of `anyio._backends._asyncio.WorkerThread.run` (skip with a clear reason if absent), and note the private-API coupling in a test comment.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T9"],"criteria":["T5e"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"monkeypatches `WorkerThread.run` to linger 0.3 s after its sentinel\"","\"the existing `importorskip(\"anyio.to_thread\")` stays\""],"finding":"The regression test monkeypatches `WorkerThread.run` in the private module `anyio/_backends/_asyncio.py`. The plan keeps only `importorskip(\"anyio.to_thread\")`, so an anyio refactor that renames or restructures `WorkerThread` would break this test with an AttributeError rather than skipping it or failing clearly.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1018e5386c6b5959","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — regression test; Portability","norm_id":"n018f704d35f22065","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An anyio upgrade moves `WorkerThread` and the regression test errors in CI for an unrelated change."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Narrow the threads `_drive_on_fresh_thread` joins to those the drive started for anyio, for example new threads that are `isinstance(t, anyio._backends._asyncio.WorkerThread)`. Do not join every newly enumerated thread. State this filter in the Approach.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T6","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.net-mechanism","project.portability"],"criteria":["E3","E5"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"record `threading.enumerate()` before starting the drive thread; after it joins, join every thread that is new since then (the anyio workers it started)\"","\"Seen in `make verify` ... (host load ~16; 1 failed, 21,400 passed)\" — the test runs inside a large shared-process suite."],"finding":"Joining 'every thread that is new since then' via a threading.enumerate() diff is broader than the plan's stated target, which is 'the anyio workers it started'. It can also catch unrelated threads started during the drive window, such as an executor or background thread left over from an earlier test in the same pytest process. If such a long-lived thread is caught, the helper waits the full 10 s bound and then fails the test. That swaps one source of flakiness for another.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f23d095477b42ba2d","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — \"join every thread that is new since then (the anyio workers it started), with a 10 s join bound\"","norm_id":"n45d8ffc56abe1dee","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An earlier test leaves a ThreadPoolExecutor whose worker spawns while this drive is running. The diff includes that worker, the join waits 10 s, and the test fails with a stuck-thread error that has nothing to do with anyio."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"After the drive thread joins, compute `new = [t for t in threading.enumerate() if t not in before and isinstance(t, WorkerThread)]`. Join each one with a 10 s timeout and assert `not t.is_alive()`. Then `del new` before `gc.collect()`.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] After each bounded join, assert `not t.is_alive()` with a message naming the wedged worker thread.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T9"],"criteria":["E6","E2"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.6,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"with a 10 s join bound so a wedged worker fails the test instead of hanging\""],"finding":"`Thread.join(timeout=10)` returns silently on timeout. The plan says a wedged worker \"fails the test instead of hanging\" but specifies no assertion that would produce that failure. Without it, a still-alive worker just falls through to the misleading `loop is None` assertion.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f9ac1a81b1d672dd1","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — \"with a 10 s join bound so a wedged worker fails the test\"","norm_id":"n8740012ea8c6e918","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A worker never receives or processes its sentinel; the join times out and the test reports the original closed-loop assertion instead of 'worker did not exit'."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"`t.join(timeout=10); assert not t.is_alive(), f\"anyio worker {t.name} did not exit within 10s\"`","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Sequence the work as: add the regression test against the unmodified helper, run it and record the failing assertion (RED), then apply the helper fix and record the pass (GREEN).","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T9"],"criteria":["E6","F1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.5371,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"A regression test that delays `WorkerThread` exit fails on the old helper and passes on the new one.\"","\"fails before the fix (RED) and passes after\""],"finding":"AC2 requires the regression test to fail on the old helper, but the plan gives no proving step for the RED state. The test is added in the same change as the fixed helper, so the RED evidence only exists if the test is run against the unmodified helper first and that result is recorded.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fea5e43fa515f4b32","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Testing / Acceptance Criteria — AC2","norm_id":"n543a723143dbff5c","priority":0.0629,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer commits the fix and the test together, and the RED claim is never observed."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1429,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the default: parametrize the lingering-worker regression test over both `completed` and `raised` outcomes.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T9"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.6,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"Add a regression test that monkeypatches `WorkerThread.run`... and asserts the loop is still collected\""],"finding":"The plan does not say which drive outcome the regression test covers. The flaky failure is in the `raised` case, but the helper serves both `completed` and `raised`, so a single-case test leaves the other path unpinned.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa7b147fc464220b5","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Testing — \"Add a regression test\"","norm_id":"n8e56be4525e02b39","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The regression test exercises only `completed` and passes, while the `raised` path stays unproven."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Reuse the existing parametrize ids (`completed`, `raised`) on the new regression test.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2857,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Limit the post-drive join to the new threads that are anyio WorkerThread instances (e.g. `isinstance(t, anyio._backends._asyncio.WorkerThread)`), not every thread that appeared since the snapshot, so unrelated threads can't cause a spurious 10 s join timeout.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.6,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: \"record `threading.enumerate()` before starting the drive thread; after it joins, join every thread that is new since then (the anyio workers it started)\"","tests/unit/test_model_classes.py:454-456 — the helper's own drive thread is the only thread it deliberately starts; anything else that shows up in the diff is uncontrolled.","The root cause names anyio's `WorkerThread` (anyio/_backends/_asyncio.py) as the only object holding the loop, so filtering by that class picks exactly the right threads."],"finding":"Joining 'every thread that is new since' a threading.enumerate() snapshot is a proxy for 'the anyio workers this drive started'. Any unrelated thread started in the same process during the drive window also gets joined. If that thread is long-lived (a background pool or watcher left by an earlier test or fixture in a long `make verify` run), the 10 s bound expires and the test fails for reasons that have nothing to do with the loop. That swaps one intermittent failure for another. Selecting threads by type, keeping only new threads that are instances of anyio's WorkerThread, or tagging them by name, joins exactly the threads the plan has shown to hold the loop.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4c5974d6a547aa0c","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — \"join every thread that is new since then (the anyio workers it started), with a 10 s join bound\"","norm_id":"n923b55fec74af209","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["In a long single-process `make verify` run (~21k tests), a background thread started by an earlier test spawns a long-lived thread while the drive is running. The helper joins it, the 10 s bound expires, and the test fails.","A future change makes the helper or the code under test start some other long-lived thread. The new-thread diff catches it and the test starts failing for a reason unrelated to the loop."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"After `thread.join()`, compute `new = [t for t in threading.enumerate() if t not in before and isinstance(t, WorkerThread)]`, where WorkerThread is imported from anyio._backends._asyncio. Join each with `t.join(10)` and assert `not t.is_alive()`, then `del new` before returning the weakref.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.4444,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] In the regression test, assert that the patched `WorkerThread.run` wrapper actually ran and lingered (e.g., a call counter > 0 after the drive), so a silent no-op patch fails instead of passing trivially.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.9,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: \"Add a regression test that monkeypatches `WorkerThread.run` to linger 0.3 s after its sentinel and asserts the loop is still collected.\"","Partially-verified: resolve_symbol reports `anyio._backends._asyncio.WorkerThread` EXISTS, but the dotted `WorkerThread.run` path came back UNRESOLVED and the source in site-packages is not readable from the repo. The only evidence for this surface is the plan's scratch reproduction.","The plan names no guard (such as a call counter or a `hasattr` check) showing the lingering wrapper actually ran."],"finding":"The regression test monkeypatches the private `anyio._backends._asyncio.WorkerThread.run` method. If a future anyio renames or restructures it, the patch may never be applied, or the worker may not linger, and nothing would detect that. The test would then pass against both the old and new helper, so the RED check would be meaningless.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1c5821ab44bf7f20","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Testing — regression test that monkeypatches `WorkerThread.run`","norm_id":"n2c4af7df02ed8c8f","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A later anyio release (the floor is anyio>=4.15) moves the worker loop out of `WorkerThread.run`. `monkeypatch.setattr` still succeeds on the class, but the wrapper never runs, the worker exits promptly, and the regression test passes on the old, racy helper too."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Have the wrapper increment a counter (or set a threading.Event) after the original `run` returns and before the 0.3 s sleep. After `_drive_on_fresh_thread` returns, assert the counter is >= 1, then assert `loop_ref() is None`. Use `monkeypatch.setattr(WorkerThread, \"run\", wrapper)` without `raising=False`, so a missing attribute fails loudly.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.3889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"insufficient","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation"